※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4582

※ A record travels as the several values it is made of, so reading or writing
※ one is that many accesses.  Which of them the ordering belonged to would have
※ no answer, and ordering all of them is a different promise from the one the
※ word makes.  Order one field and let the rest be ordinary.

type Pair = a : u32 ; b : u32

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let q: mut Pair = Pair(.a ← 1u32, .b ← 2u32)
    if ⎕acquire(&q).a = 1u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
